{"kind":"assert","text":"Pre-review of exact resident-repair head 1843fd90 found one test-portability blocker. internal/app/resident_test.go's unreadable-record subtest applies chmod 0000 but does not check whether the running process can still read the file. Privileged Unix processes can bypass those mode bits, and Windows chmod does not make the file unreadable; the test can therefore fail without exercising the intended open-error branch. The sibling CLI fixture already has the correct shape: attempt the read after chmod and loudly skip when the environment cannot exercise unreadability. The internal/app fixture must use the same explicit check before this head can be approved."}